The other side of the escaping rules. None of these characters begins markdown
where it sits, thus none of them may grow a backslash:

  `#` and `-` and `+` and `=` in the middle of a line, and never at its start
  `&` with no name and `;` after it, thus `AT&T` is not a character entity
  `<` before a number, thus `<3` opens no autolink and no HTML tag
  `_` between two letters or numbers, thus `snake_case_name` is one word
  `|` outside a table, where it divides nothing

An escaper that is safe but not narrow would write `issue \#42` and `AT\&T`.
A reader shows those the same way, thus the damage is only to the source, and
`md format` writes that source into the file of everybody who runs it.
